        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under Schlenk/glove-box conditions, YbCp2 (0.41 g, 1.35 mmol) and Hg(pzPh)2 (0.37 g, 0.75 mmol) were stirred in THF. After two days the mixture turned pale orange with precipitation of Hg0. After filtration from the metal residue and exposure to vacuum, a yellow–orange oily residue remained. The oil was washed with hexane and dried under vacuum to a yellow powder. Dissolution in THF and slow solvent removal produced one large orange crystal of 1 (~1–4% yield). The remaining powder was identified as [Yb(Cp)(pzPh)(thf)] (0.18 g, 26%).",
