        "procedure": "THF (40 mL) was added to a Schlenk flask charged with excess freshly filed Nd metal (0.30 g, 2.8 mmol), bis(pentafluorophenyl)mercury (0.30 g, 0.54 mmol), and o-PhPhFormH (0.30 g, 0.86 mmol) under purified nitrogen. The slurry was stirred at ambient temperature for 72 h. The colourless–yellow solution was filtered from elemental mercury and excess Nd. Solvent was removed under vacuum and the residue extracted into THF (5 mL), concentrated to ~2 mL, and stored at −6 °C for several weeks to give blue square-shaped crystals of 2 (0.25 g, 51%).",
