        "procedure": "Europium metal (excess, 0.54 g, 3.5 mmol), Hg(C6F5)2 (0.24 g, 0.46 mmol), and FFormH (0.21 g, 0.92 mmol) were sonicated in THF (20 mL) for one day. The solution was filtered from metal residues and evaporated to dryness under vacuum. The fluoro yellow powder was washed with toluene then hexane and dissolved in diglyme (5 mL); during this process the Schlenk flask was briefly exposed to air. After storage at −40 °C for 18 months, two small yellow crystals of 3 were obtained (~1–4% yield) and used for synchrotron X-ray analysis.",
